
  Proceeding with my own approaches.

  [1mApproaches for the change-event seam[0m

  This is the one genuinely architectural choice left, because it decides what notifications can ever be built on top.

  [1mA. State is truth, events are a side channel (recommended).[0m [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m holds the current array of tasks. Every
  mutation goes through a small store module that writes the new state [3mand[0m appends a change record ([38;5;153m{id, type, taskId, [39m
  [38;5;153mat, fields}[39m) to a capped log. Notifications read the log.
  - [3mBuys:[0m dead simple to reason about; rendering reads state directly; the log can be truncated or dropped without data
    loss.
  - [3mCosts:[0m the log can drift from state if someone writes [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m directly — prevented by making the store the only
    writer.
  - [3mRules out:[0m nothing important. A server can append to the same log later.

  [1mB. Event-sourced — the log is truth.[0m Only events are stored; current state is a fold over the log at load time.
  - [3mBuys:[0m perfect history, undo, and audit for free; a natural fit if sync arrives later (events merge better than
    snapshots).
  - [3mCosts:[0m every read replays the log; you need snapshotting once the log grows; a bad event shape is now a migration
    problem, not a cleanup.
  - [3mWhen it wins:[0m if undo/history is a headline feature, or multi-device sync is a near-term certainty.

  [1mC. No log — derive changes by diffing snapshots.[0m Keep the previous task array, diff on write.
  - [3mBuys:[0m least code; nothing extra to store.
  - [3mCosts:[0m diffing loses intent (a title edit and a retitle-plus-complete look alike), and it can't represent anything
    that happened while the tab was closed.
  - [3mRules out:[0m meaningful notification text. I'd avoid this.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It gives notifications a real, intentional event stream at almost no extra cost, keeps rendering
  trivial, and leaves B reachable later (the log is already there — you'd just promote it to source of truth).

  Does A sound right, or does undo/history matter enough to pull you toward B?

